# Capacitor.js Mobile Development

## Speculative / not a confirmed part of Rhynk's stack

**Capacitor is not installed and not mentioned anywhere in Rhynk's actual
product docs** (`docs/Rhynk_PRD_v2.2.pdf`, `docs/rhynk_hld.pdf`,
`docs/rhynk_lld.pdf`, `docs/AUTH_MODULE.md`). There is no
`@capacitor/core` in `package.json`, no `capacitor.config.*` in the repo,
and no evidence of a planned native-mobile-hybrid strategy for this
project. This file is **deferred, speculative reference only** — patterns
to fall back on *if* the team later decides to wrap this web client in
Capacitor for Android/iOS distribution. Don't import from any `@capacitor/*`
package, don't build UI that branches on `isNative()`/`isMobile()`, and
don't treat anything below as already wired up. If Capacitor is adopted,
that's a deliberate, separate decision to record in `00-project-overview.mdc`
and `package.json` first.

The code patterns below are otherwise generic (platform detection, touch
targets, safe-area insets) and harmless to keep as a reference for that
hypothetical future — just don't act on them today.

## Capacitor.js Integration (if adopted)

### Platform Detection
```javascript
// src/utils/platform.utils.js
import { Capacitor } from '@capacitor/core'

export const isNative = () => Capacitor.isNativePlatform()
export const isWeb = () => !Capacitor.isNativePlatform()
export const getPlatform = () => Capacitor.getPlatform()

export const isIOS = () => getPlatform() === 'ios'
export const isAndroid = () => getPlatform() === 'android'
export const isMobile = () => isIOS() || isAndroid()

// Usage in components
const ResponsiveComponent = () => {
  return (
    <div>
      {isMobile() ? <MobileLayout /> : <DesktopLayout />}
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Device Information
```javascript
// src/hooks/useDeviceInfo.js
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react'
import { Device } from '@capacitor/device'

const useDeviceInfo = () => {
  const [deviceInfo, setDeviceInfo] = useState(null)
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)

  useEffect(() => {
    const getDeviceInfo = async () => {
      try {
        const info = await Device.getInfo()
        setDeviceInfo(info)
      } catch (error) {
        console.error('Failed to get device info:', error)
      } finally {
        setLoading(false)
      }
    }

    getDeviceInfo()
  }, [])

  return { deviceInfo, loading }
}

export default useDeviceInfo
```

